{"id": "JAH-SIG-SECUREEX-000001", "slug": "tool-secure-execution-sandbox-signature", "title": "Secure Execution Sandbox \u2014 Overview and definition", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "tool database record", "ladder_rank": 1, "body": "Signature edition. Original Signature methods and framings developed for the JAH system, labeled Signature throughout. Restricts programs to controlled resources and permissions. The Secure Execution Sandbox runs untrusted or semi-trusted code inside strict boundaries: limited CPU and memory, no network by default, filesystem access to a scratch area only, and a deny-list of dangerous operations. Every blocked attempt is logged. It lets code run without letting it roam. Defensive isolation \u2014 a containment tool. Capability specification and design target: this database describes what the tool must do, not a claim of implementation or deployment. Defensive and engineering content only \u2014 no weapon-targeting or attack-execution content.", "capabilities": ["CPU, memory, and time limits", "Filesystem confinement to scratch areas", "Network deny-by-default", "Dangerous-operation blocking with logs", "Violation reporting"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Tool overview and capability inventory", "code": "J({tool:TOOL.name,capabilities:TOOL.capabilities,count:TOOL.capabilities.length});assert(TOOL.capabilities.length>=5,'caps');", "verified_output": "{\"tool\":\"Secure Execution Sandbox\",\"capabilities\":[\"CPU, memory, and time limits\",\"Filesystem confinement to scratch areas\",\"Network deny-by-default\",\"Dangerous-operation blocking with logs\",\"Violation reporting\"],\"count\":5}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "catalog-100-darpa-nasa-grade-tools-2026-10-21.txt", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_n